   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What did not happen",
     "texto": [
      "To say «if (I) had done something…» about something that can no longer be changed, use **-았/었더라면**: 가다 → **갔더라면** (if (I) had gone), 먹다 → **먹었더라면** (if (I) had eaten), 알다 → **알았더라면** (if (I) had known it).",
      "어제 왔**더라면** 재미있었을 거예요 = if you had come yesterday, it would have been fun."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "With the result",
     "texto": [
      "Afterwards **-았/었을 텐데** or **-았/었을 거예요** is usually used to say what would have happened: 미리 알았더라면 갔을 텐데 = if I had known in advance, I would have gone.",
      "It is a feeling of regret, of «what a shame»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
